---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CallLink from "../components/CallLink.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Water damage and homeowners insurance in Georgia"
  description="What Georgia homeowners usually photograph, tell the adjuster, and ask a restoration company after a burst pipe, leak, or storm."
>
  <article class="hero wrap">
    <h1>Insurance after water in the house</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This is not legal advice and we do not file claims. It is what Gwinnett
      homeowners run into after a pipe, appliance, or storm leak.
    </p>
  </article>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Often covered</h2>
    <p>
      A sudden burst pipe, a failed supply line, a water heater that lets go,
      or a washing-machine hose that splits. Those are the jobs carriers see
      every week. “Sudden and accidental” is the phrase they use.
    </p>
    <h2>Often not covered — or only with an add-on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A leak you knew about and left for months</li>
      <li>Flood from a creek, street, or rising groundwater (that is flood insurance)</li>
      <li>Sewer backup, unless you bought that endorsement</li>
      <li>Wear and tear, a rusted water heater you never replaced, poor maintenance</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Read your declarations page or call the agent. The restoration company
      can tell you what they usually see approved. They cannot promise your
      carrier will pay.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What to have ready</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Photos of every wet room, the source if you can see it, and anything you had to throw out.</li>
      <li>A short written list: when you found it, what you shut off, who has been in the house.</li>
      <li>Your policy number and the carrier’s claim line.</li>
      <li>If a crew is coming, tell them you plan to file so they document moisture readings.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What we do and do not do</h2>
    <p>
      Call or send the form. The company that helps you may bill insurance
      directly. You still choose whether to hire them.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/#request">Request help</a>
      <CallLink class="btn secondary" />
      <a class="btn secondary" href="/what-to-do">First-hour checklist</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
